WEBVTT

00:00:00.138 --> 00:00:02.800
Deploying a detection is an operational change.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.760
Teams should consider whether the detection will alert immediately,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.845
whether it should run silently first, and who will monitor early behavior.

00:00:08.845 --> 00:00:11.555
A rollout should also define which playbook applies,

00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:15.595
how analysts will interpret the signal, and how unexpected alert volume will be handled.

00:00:15.595 --> 00:00:17.240
Careful deployment reduces surprise.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.490
It gives teams a chance to understand real-world behavior before relying on the detection

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.170
fully.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.260
Managed rollout also supports trust.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.930
Analysts are more likely to use a new detection well when they understand its purpose,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.560
severity, expected context, and escalation path.
